- op: discuss  # 0ae8
  at: '2026-04-17T01:02:15Z'  # 0ae8
  by: agent  # 0ae8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0ae8
  clock: 3  # 0ae8
  nonce: 0ae8  # 0ae8
  message: "Withdrawing this filing and re-filing as a work_item audit per self-review (2026-04-17).\n\nRe-analysis surfaced seven major issues with this item as filed:\n\n1. Status 'violated' was premature — the inconsistency claim rests on inference from grep output, not verification. I never read framework_patterns.py or a sample YAML before filing. The actual failure mode could be (a) shape is consistent and one side is simply broken, (b) there's a normalization step I haven't inspected, (c) my reading of the grep was wrong. An invariant with status=violated should cite a verified concrete symptom, not a logical chain.\n\n2. Two distinct concerns conflated: Problem 1 (data-shape inconsistency, a possible defect) and Problem 2 (producer/consumer coupling is undocumented, a visibility/drift concern). These have different severity, evidence bars, and fixes — they belong in separate items.\n\n3. Acceptance criteria overreach the filing. Some ACs (test infrastructure that grep-matches linker filters against YAML concept emissions; docs/CONCEPTS.md existing and 'not a stub') are separate deliverables bundled into one item.\n\n4. Phase 2 was prescriptive about the canonical shape (list[dict] with mandatory 'concept' field) before any audit. The shape should emerge from evidence, not be pre-decided.\n\n5. Line-number citations (~81, ~86, ~305, etc.) are fragile. Code will move; the tilde concedes fragility without fixing it.\n\n6. Tag 'cross_language_linkers' is wrong for this item — this is a FRAMEWORK_PATTERNS/linker contract concern, mostly within-language. Inherited-by-habit from the conflation we just spent six PRs correcting.\n\n7. No cited user-facing symptom. No failing test, bug report, bakeoff finding, or tracker item where the conjectured inconsistency has been observed. An invariant marked 'violated' with no symptom is speculation, however structurally plausible.\n\nResolution: setting status to 'deleted' and re-filing Problem 1 (as a focused audit work_item) separately from Problem 2 (which may or may not warrant its own item pending audit outcome). The replacement work_item will cite this INV for context."  # 0ae8
